  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "Mix ingredients except vitamin solution, NaHCO3, Na2S·9H2O and cysteine-HCl, and autoclave under a H2/CO2 (80/20) atmosphere. Separately autoclave cysteine-HCl and Na2S·9H2O as 5% solutions under a N2 atmosphere. Sterilize vitamin and 8% NaHCO3 solutions by filtration. Prior to inoculation, aseptically and anaerobically add vitamin, NaHCO3, cysteine-HCl and Na2S·9H2O solutions. Pressurize the inoculated bottles to 150 kPa with H2/CO2."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "Dissolve nitrilotoriacetic acid and adjust pH to 6.5 with KOH. Then add minerals. Adjust final pH to 7.0."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
}